Will Tournament have an Australian server?

Last year was so much fun I hope somebody can run an Australian server
this year for the Nethack Tournament. The lag overseas will be too
much of a barrier otherwise, so I say for all Australian players this
is essential.

I'd love to pit my skills against the world again. It adds an
indescribable extra thrill to the game to be competing worldwide. Last
year was my first time ever to play via telnet, my first time ever to
play the current version of the game, my first time ever to play via
idiosynchratic controls varying from the windows vanilla port, my
first time ever in the tournament. I was drunk and stoned each time I
logged on, yet I managed to take my first character "Fatdick" through
to ascension. IIRC 2nd or 3rd in the australian standings, 42nd on the
world scoreboard.

I desperately want to enter the comp again and I grovel at the shoes
of anyone willing to run a server in Aust to make this possible. If u
do, you are a winner already.

